documen�ng these⏎founda�on models (or other types of issues and the steps it has taken to address them in its transparency documenta�on (e.g.,⏎machine learning models or solu�ons), transparency notes, system cards and product documenta�on).⏎such as AI pla�orms, that are suitable for⏎specific healthcare problems and data⏎sources.⏎Digital Health Someone who creates complete digital Building on the cross-AI/ML Developer roles noted above:⏎tools and technologies to improve health • Specifying appropriate uses for its digital health solu�on to avoid amplifying bias or safety issues that⏎Solu�on Developer⏎and healthcare outcomes, such as may exist in the underlying founda�on models, AI pla�orms, or health AI pla�orms.⏎providing diagnos�c and administra�ve • Designing user interfaces to enable an end user to safely and effec�vely act upon the output of the⏎solu�ons for clinicians, pa�ents, and tool, such as providing explana�ons, feedback mechanisms, or human oversight op�ons, providing⏎healthcare organiza�ons. They may build clear documenta�on to Deploying Organiza�ons and Users to help them avoid bias and safety issues.⏎digital health solu�ons with both health⏎AI pla�orms, which are specialized for the⏎health care domain, and AI pla�orms,⏎which are more general and adaptable for⏎various use cases and applica�ons.⏎6⏎⏎NIST AI RMF⏎Stakeholder Group Defini�on Roles⏎Actor Tasks⏎Deploying Someone who is a healthcare Respecting that managing AI/ML risks will be more challenging for small to Assessment; Procurement;⏎Organiza�on providers and health care payors that medium-sized organizations depending on their capabilities and resources: Governance and Oversight⏎(Healthcare Provider and is deploying solu�ons built by • Adop�ng AI/ML Developer instruc�ons for use, specifying appropriate uses⏎or Payor) Digital Health Solu�on Developers. for Users through governance policies to avoid bias and safety issues that⏎They may also have their own internal may exist in the underlying found